2. Fluency: perplexity under an independent judge (google/gemma-4-E2B-it)
==============================================================================
The judge must be a different model. Scoring watermarked text with the model
that produced it is biased against it by construction: SynthID selects among
near-ties using the g-function rather than raw probability, so watermarked
text sits slightly off that model's own argmax path regardless of quality.
A different-sized sibling has different weights and a different argmax path,
so it does not inherit that bias, though it does share a tokenizer and
training lineage -- an independent architecture would be a stronger control.
creative     n=  96  PPL wm 17.789 vs un 17.395  diff +0.394 [-0.557,+1.355]  no significant difference
open_ended   n=  96  PPL wm 5.480 vs un 5.511  diff -0.030 [-0.268,+0.203]  no significant difference
financial    n=  96  PPL wm 5.694 vs un 5.686  diff +0.008 [-0.399,+0.449]  no significant difference
